NOTE: This story has 13 acceptance criteria — MANDATORY split required (see SPLIT RULES below).

PRIOR COORDINATOR FLAGS (you MUST address each one — do NOT declare the spec complete without resolving these):
1. AC count is 13 at splitDepth=1 — exceeds 12-AC limit; speckit flagged this and recommended consolidating GATE-CONTENT-TYPE into GATE-INPUT-400; human decision required before implementation
2. Verdict format ('Verdict: <TOKEN>' colon-prefix) is consistent with SKY-006-a sibling but inconsistent with promoted split children SKY-006-A-1 and SKY-006-B-1 (bare ^(PASS|FAIL)$) — human clarification required on which child set is canonical; this story may be superseded
3. .gitignore requirement added to GATE-SECRET by speckit — reasonable security addition but was not explicitly human-approved as a policy decision; implementers should confirm this is intentional
4. GATE-ENV-CONFIG is a new gate added by speckit that was not in the original coordinator routing — it covers a genuine gap (startup validation of required env vars) but was added without explicit coordinator approval; human confirmation recommended
5. ARTEFACT AC now enumerates eleven sections but VERDICT AC references 'all gates enumerated in the ARTEFACT AC' — this self-referential enumeration pattern is correct but fragile; any future gate addition requires updating both ARTEFACT and VERDICT
6. This story may be superseded by SKY-006-B-1 (promoted split child) — human clarification required on which child set is canonical implementation path

Additional context from prior review: Both openspec and speckit contributed genuine, non-overlapping value. openspec fixed the ARTEFACT VCS commitment requirement (removed 'committed to the repository' — operationally unsatisfiable for /tmp writes), fixed the gate count mismatch in VERDICT (was 'ten sub-checks' with only some gates enumerated), added GATE-ASYNC-EXPRESS-ERROR to GATE-ERROR-HANDLING, added GATE-CORS with explicit pass/fail criteria, conditioned GATE-PATH-SAFETY symlink resolution on presence of manual static-file serv

Generate refined acceptance criteria, optionally updated title/description, and split stories where required. Output JSON only between <SPEC_AGENT> tags using this schema:
